$$
将 $t = \frac{1}{x}$，则 $\lim_{x \to +\infty} \frac{2}{x} = 0$。
$$
\lim_{x \to +\infty} x\left[f\left(2+\frac{2}{x}\right)-f(2)\right] = \lim_{t \to 0} \frac{f(2+2t)-f(2)}{t}
$$
由于 $f(x)$ 由参数方程 $\left\{\begin{array}{l}x=1+t^{3} \\ y=e^{t^{2}}\end{array}\right.$ 确定，因此 $f(x) = e^{x^2/3}$。
$$
\lim_{t \to 0} \frac{f(2+2t)-f(2)}{t} = \lim_{t \to 0} \frac{e^{(2+2t)^2/3}-e^{2^2/3}}{t} = \lim_{t \to 0} \frac{e^{(4+8t+4t^2)/3}-e^{4/3}}{t}
$$
$$
= \lim_{t \to 0} \frac{e^{4/3}(e^{8t/3}-1)}{t} \cdot e^{4/3} = e^{4/3} \lim_{t \to 0} \frac{e^{8t/3}-1}{t}
$$
$$
= e^{4/3} \lim_{t \to 0} \frac{8}{3} \frac{e^{8t/3}}{(8t/3)} = e^{4/3} \cdot \frac{8}{3} \cdot \frac{3}{8} = e^{4/3}
$$
因此，$\lim _{x \rightarrow+\infty} x\left[f\left(2+\frac{2}{x}\right)-f(2)\right] = e^{4/3}$.

